// The marketplace on Cloudflare (Workers static assets — what Cloudflare now calls Pages), 20-Sep-2026.
// The `assets` block serves web/dist-market as-is. What reaches the script in workers/market.js
// (release R6, 24-Sep-2026, revised after review) is decided by Cloudflare's router, in this order:
//   a path that IS a file               the asset layer: free, unlimited, no invocation (every chunk, font,
//                                       icon, sw.js, version.json)
//   a NAVIGATION to an unknown path     index.html from the asset layer (`single-page-application`), free,
//   (Sec-Fetch-Mode: navigate)          no invocation — assets_navigation_prefers_asset_serving, default
//                                       since compatibility date 2025-04-01
//   any other unknown path              the Worker: /api/market[?ref=] (a fetch, never a navigation) → the
//                                       Render origin through the Cache API — fresh 60 s, stale-while-
//                                       revalidate, the last good copy when the origin is cold or down, a
//                                       404 forwarded when the store is closed; a missing chunk or font
//                                       (a script/font fetch is not a navigation) → a real 404 + no-store
//                                       instead of index.html + "immutable"; anything else → the binding's
//                                       own SPA answer
// There is deliberately NO run_worker_first. The first R6 cut listed /api/*, /assets/* and /fonts/*:
// every chunk request was then a billed invocation and, past the Workers Free cap (100k/day), a 429
// instead of the file — the whole store down until the daily reset. And listing ONLY /api/* does not
// work either: any run_worker_first array turns on "static routing", under which the asset layer's
// SPA fallback answers every miss itself (index.html + immutable for a missing chunk, the audit's
// D-10) and the Worker never sees it — read in the shared router (@cloudflare/workers-shared
// asset-worker canFetch: has_static_routing keeps not_found_handling for the existence check) and
// verified in wrangler dev on all three configurations, 24-Sep-2026. /api/market needs no rule: it
// is not a file, so a fetch of it reaches the Worker by the miss path. Budget and the cliff: the
// header of workers/market.js.
// Response headers for static files come from public/_headers, copied into the build root by Vite; the
// Worker sets its own headers on what it answers itself.
// Deploy: python -m scripts.deploy_cf market (builds first) or .github/workflows/cf-deploy.yml; a
// release uploads a version and switches traffic with `wrangler versions deploy` (docs/RELEASE.md),
// so a rollback is the previous version @100%.
// `routes` with custom_domain attach the hostnames: wrangler creates the DNS records and the
// certificate in the zone (same account) on deploy.
{
  "name": "yq-marketplace",
  "main": "workers/market.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-18",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist-market",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application"
  },
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "yqmarketplace.com", "custom_domain": true },
    { "pattern": "www.yqmarketplace.com", "custom_domain": true }
  ],
  "workers_dev": true,
  // Workers Logs (free tier: 200k events/day, 3-day retention): one invocation event per request that
  // reaches the script — /api/market and the odd missing chunk, the same small set as the budget —
  // plus the Worker's own console line on an origin timeout/error (nothing per hit), so the volume is
  // tiny and a cold-origin day is visible.
  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
